{{ orders_json }}

If the customer's message identifies one or more specific orders from this list, call resolve_redemption_orders with their order_refs - including a count/aggregate question like "how many coins are yet to be delivered" or "which ones were attempted", which should resolve to every matching order, not just one. A "track"/"where is" style request that narrows by product or type (e.g. "track my gold coin") but still matches more than one is NOT resolved - call no_single_redemption_match instead, with matching_order_refs set to the narrowed matches, so the customer picks one from just those rather than every ongoing order. You must call exactly one of these two tools - never answer in plain text, and never describe, list, or summarize the orders yourself.
